From 0b6c7e5723896b4a3e2b361ec049acb8c5c5560c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vili Kohonen <vili.kohonen@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:40:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Stop a run on a defective-grader fraction, from two signals,
 averaged over a window

The per-batch share is max(arbitrary_pass, lambda), as before. The trigger is now the mean
of that share over the last `window` batches reaching `frac`, replacing `frac` held for
`sustain_steps` consecutive batches: a converged run on the January-2026 parameters keeps
5-16% of rollouts at the length cap with no grader, so its batch share wobbles 0.83-0.96
and a streak rule never fires. 0.90 over 5 fires on all 26 cached runs that hacked and on
none of the 16 that did not.
